q=dict(question='With a full snapshot pending on a voter using AsyncStorageWrites, can completion of older normal-entry application work allow an explicit Campaign before the snapshot append response is delivered?',importance='Campaigning before the pending recovery barrier is released could let authority acquisition use a restored log/configuration while local snapshot work remains incomplete. The selected discriminator concerns local campaign admission; an election win, conflicting decision or client-visible consequence would require independent history and observations.',disposition='needs_specific_evidence',preferred_check='controlled_schedule',participants=['Elected leader and quorum follower producing a snapshot prefix','Lagging voter receiving a full snapshot','Serialized RawNode caller and separate FIFO append/apply workers'],objects=['Pending snapshot identity','Previously issued normal-entry apply batch and attached response','Campaign request','Term, role and outbound vote requests'],contexts=['Three fixed voters with all bootstrap configuration entries applied','AsyncStorageWrites and no pre-vote; explicit Campaign, without election timer assumptions','Snapshot produced from an actually committed and applied leader prefix after the receiving voter is isolated','Older apply batch contains only normal entries; complete it before state-machine snapshot installation','No restart, configuration transition or critical raft-state assignment'],event_paths=['Proposal and replication -> leader application -> MemoryStorage.CreateSnapshot and Compact -> automatic snapshot fallback -> follower full restore','Earlier MsgStorageApply work -> apply normal entries -> attached MsgStorageApplyResp -> explicit Campaign while snapshot append work remains held','Complete snapshot storage and installation -> attached MsgStorageAppendResp -> repeat Campaign with a fixed output drain'],activity_classes=['A2','A3','A5','A6'],behavior_ids=list(edges),fact_ids=[newid],supporting_behavior_ids={'B_propose_replicate':'Actual missing-predecessor replication path produces MsgSnap from leader storage.','B_aggregate_commit':'Quorum commitment establishes the producer prefix from which the application creates the snapshot.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['promotable directly tests hasNextOrInProgressSnapshot, while MsgStorageApplyResp only changes applied progress; source review predicts the barrier remains intact.','Ready acceptance changes snapshotInProgress but leaves the pointer used by the guard present.','Snapshot fast-forward when its index/term already matches the recipient log does not create the selected pending barrier and must be distinguished in construction.'],unknowns=['Establish a producer-derived full-restore history with a genuine earlier normal-entry apply batch still outstanding.','Determine the applicable local campaign responsibility and independent observations without treating Campaign return nil as election admission.','Broader snapshot/state-machine ordering remains unresolved for older configuration batches; that case is excluded from this discriminator.'],trigger_rationale='The prior source handoff separated applied-index advancement from snapshot completion. A single actual pending snapshot with an older normal apply response isolates the consumer guard with fewer caller-contract assumptions than overlapping configuration application or replacement snapshots. Compare term/role/vote output for Campaign while held and after completed snapshot work; controls should finish under a fixed schedule rather than await an election win.')
