s=dict(action='continue',rationale='Map the distinct recovery barrier and select a bounded authority-admission question. Preserve the unresolved cross-target state-machine configuration contract as a limitation instead of inventing an obligation.',map_path='snapshot-support-map.json',map_changes=changes,question=q,feedback=dict(ref_ids=['S_async_usage','S_restore_config','S_log_snapshot','S_step','S_apply_progress','S_memory_snapshot','S_transfer_snapshot_test'],answered='The pending snapshot pointer, not applied index or snapshotInProgress alone, is the shared object linking full recovery to campaign admission and next committed-entry delivery. Full restore produces it, Ready retains it in progress, ordinary apply responses do not clear it, and matching-index snapshot completion retires it. The new map records these distinct direct edges under their existing activity ownership. The transfer test supplies an adjacent expectation, not execution of this question.',remaining=['Construct the actual full-restore prefix and older normal application batch through public RawNode and storage APIs.','Fix the local duty and an independent Campaign-admission oracle before formal execution.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The current code guard is concrete counterevidence to premature admission. A controlled public-entry history can discriminate whether that guard survives real asynchronous handoffs, while avoiding the unsettled configuration/application ordering branch.'))
